Bugfix: Close the header menus when the focus leaves them

The app menu and the user menu of the signed-in layout stayed open when the
tab key carried the focus out of them. They closed on a mouse click only, and
escape no longer reached them because its handler sits on the menu and on the
toggle. The open panel is fixed above the app sidebar, so the sidebar entry
that held the focus showed a ten pixel strip of itself and nothing else.

Both menus now close as soon as the focus leaves the toggle and the menu. The
focus is not pulled back to the toggle, it moves on to where the tab key sent
it. Escape, the mouse and the pointer behaviour are unchanged.

WCAG 2.2 AAA, SC 2.4.12
